#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073635 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073724 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a94905c-48fe-5662-bb6c-2153f7725648" :knowledge-point/title "Problem Solving Using the Ratio of Two Integers"}] :question/id #uuid "a86fdc21-1c98-5929-8282-aed055b1b053" :question/math-academy-id "e-4745" :question/problem "If a machine at a factory takes $6$ hours to complete $2$ batches of refractory bricks, how many hours does it take to complete $10$ batches?" :question/worked-solution "To find the number of hours it takes the machine to complete $10$ batches of refractory bricks, we first find the unit rate of hours per batch and then multiply the unit rate by $10$ batches.\n\nTo find the unit rate of hours per batch, we divide the number of hours, $6,$ by the number of batches, $2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6÷2 & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $3$ hours per batch. To find the number of hours it takes the machine to complete $10$ batches, we multiply the unit rate by $10$ batches and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\times 10 & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the machine $30$ hours to complete $10$ batches."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073636 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea092786-a281-534e-803b-90e6c23b90a9" :knowledge-point/title "Problem Solving Using the Ratio of a Fraction and an Integer"}] :question/id #uuid "52c7bc18-eedc-504f-bbae-a501944834a0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4746" :question/problem "At a certain sports center, there are $5$ equal-size pools. If a pump can empty $\\dfrac{3}{2}$ of a pool in $15$ minutes, then how many minutes will it take the pump to empty all $5$ pools?" :question/worked-solution "To find the number of minutes that the pump takes to empty $5$ pools, we can first find the unit rate of minutes per pool, and then multiply the unit rate by $5$ pools.\n\nTo find the unit rate of minutes per pool, we divide the number of minutes, $15,$ by the total pool volume emptied, $\\dfrac{3}{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n15 \\div \\dfrac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nTo divide by a fraction, we multiply by the fraction's reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15÷\\frac{3}{2} & =15\\times \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{1}\\times \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\times 2}{1\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{3} \\\\  & =30÷3 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $10$ minutes per pool. To find the number of minutes that the pump takes to empty $5$ pools, we multiply the unit rate by $5$ pools and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10\\times 5 & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the pump will take $50$ minutes to empty $5$ pools."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073637 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d34e60c9-710b-50ca-a491-adc2b50e6edc" :knowledge-point/title "Problem Solving Using the Ratio of Two Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "4f61ec9c-9b87-5b25-9543-44b6043b7b4a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4747" :question/problem "Ava works in a coffee store. She earns a bonus of $\\dfrac 3 4$ of a dollar for each $\\dfrac 3 8$ liters of coffee sold. How much of a bonus will Ava earn if she sells $18$ liters of coffee?" :question/worked-solution "To find the number of dollars that Ava earns if she sells $18$ liters of coffee, we can first find the unit rate of dollars per liter, and then multiply the unit rate by $18$ liters.\n\nTo find the unit rate of dollars per liter, we divide the number of dollars, $\\dfrac{3}{4},$ by the number of liters, $\\dfrac{3}{8},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{4} \\div \\dfrac{3}{8}\n$$\n\nDividing one fraction by another is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of the second fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}÷\\frac{3}{8} & =\\frac{3}{4}\\times \\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 8}{4\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{12} \\\\  & =24÷12 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $2$ dollars per liter. To find the number of dollars that Ava earns selling $18$ liters, we multiply the unit rate by $18$ liters and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\times 18 & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Ava earns $36$ dollars if she sells $18$ liters of coffee."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073724 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a94905c-48fe-5662-bb6c-2153f7725648" :knowledge-point/title "Problem Solving Using the Ratio of Two Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dfef5b3-9dfe-5c33-81e3-d41a625451ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$40$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490628} {:answer/id #uuid "9b97c63c-7074-5837-8447-7f7b5f8ef14c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$34$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490831} {:answer/id #uuid "d911d5fc-58d5-5059-86e5-95360946c0d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$32$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490924} {:answer/id #uuid "e375a4ab-4a8d-5662-b6d1-09924cb00049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$38$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490945} {:answer/id #uuid "f54f889a-d359-5750-8817-1df82694220b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$36$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f54f889a-d359-5750-8817-1df82694220b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$36$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490980} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a23102f-c8ce-5244-8b2d-937f38e2f07c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "803aecb5-0c77-5ccb-b734-dbe320a2826b" :question/math-academy-id "q-148204" :question/problem "It takes Douglas $20$ minutes to shear $5$ sheep. How many minutes will it take to shear $9$ sheep?" :question/worked-solution "To determine the number of minutes it will take Douglas to shear $9$ sheep, we first find the unit rate of minutes per sheep and then multiply it by $9$ sheep.\n\nTo find the unit rate of minutes per sheep, we divide the number of minutes, $20,$ by the number of sheep, $5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20÷5 & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $4$ minutes per sheep. To find the number of minutes it takes Douglas to shear $9$ sheep, we multiply the unit rate by $9$ sheep and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\times 9 & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes Douglas $36$ minutes to shear $9$ sheep."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea092786-a281-534e-803b-90e6c23b90a9" :knowledge-point/title "Problem Solving Using the Ratio of a Fraction and an Integer"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03b2e537-c06f-570e-80d9-c69b54d5db82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490519} {:answer/id #uuid "1f6d490e-ee29-533a-9c1b-4215899df3b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490569} {:answer/id #uuid "52d29a71-945d-530d-a118-ccf4c6730562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490669} {:answer/id #uuid "8085cb4b-293b-5f54-931d-315952889efd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490769} {:answer/id #uuid "b446b045-dc82-596f-8d46-675e569a086b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52d29a71-945d-530d-a118-ccf4c6730562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490669} :answer-field/id #uuid "f90489e0-fda9-52b4-aa57-bb15b814888a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491107}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6ee32ba5-d533-567a-a32c-16aed9424364" :question/math-academy-id "q-148226" :question/problem "Laura can decorate $5$ cakes in $\\frac{5}{2}$ hours. How many cakes can she decorate in $3$ hours?" :question/worked-solution "To determine the number of cakes Laura can decorate in $3$ hours, we first find the unit rate of cakes per hour and then multiply it by $3$ hours.\n\nTo find the unit rate of cakes per hour, we divide the number of cakes, $5,$ by the number of hours, $\\frac{5}{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n5÷\\frac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nTo divide by a fraction, we multiply by the fraction's reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5÷\\frac{5}{2} & =5\\times \\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{1}\\times \\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\times 2}{1\\times 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5} \\\\  & =10÷5 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $2$ cakes per hour. To determine the number of cakes Laura can decorate in $3$ hours, we multiply the unit rate by $3$ hours and get\n\n$$\n2\\times 3=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Laura can decorate $6$ cakes in $3$ hours."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d34e60c9-710b-50ca-a491-adc2b50e6edc" :knowledge-point/title "Problem Solving Using the Ratio of Two Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d233c4d-91ce-5842-96ac-2ac9124a19b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490563} {:answer/id #uuid "1d3ecdf6-cc46-52ec-8cae-496cd449a2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490565} {:answer/id #uuid "22d4604e-a1bf-5092-88c7-d8b85fe39f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490574} {:answer/id #uuid "2f5e3729-fbf9-57ad-a68e-33e03b5eb2fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490602} {:answer/id #uuid "75455607-0ce5-5a87-92db-670bb08b604b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22d4604e-a1bf-5092-88c7-d8b85fe39f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490574} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f330a21-ae37-5b4c-b04c-2851be121d6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec888cfc-fd30-59e8-bd79-e4af221c07b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-148285" :question/problem "To make a cake mix, Eva uses $\\frac{3}{8}$ of a cup of wheat flour and $\\frac{3}{16}$ of a cup of sugar. How many cups of flour does she need if she wants to use $2$ cups of sugar?" :question/worked-solution "To determine the number of cups of flour Eva needs if she wants to use $2$ cups of sugar, we first find the unit ratio of cups of flour per cup of sugar and then multiply it by $2$ cups of sugar.\n\nTo find the unit ratio of cups of flour per cup of sugar, we divide the number of cups of flour, $\\frac{3}{8},$ by the number of cups of sugar, $\\frac{3}{16},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{8}÷\\frac{3}{16}\n$$\n\nDividing one fraction by another is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of the second fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}÷\\frac{3}{16} & =\\frac{3}{8}\\times \\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 16}{8\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{24} \\\\  & =48÷24 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $2$ cups of flour per cup of sugar. To determine the number of cups of flour Eva needs if she wants to use $2$ cups of sugar, we multiply the unit rate by $2$ cups of sugar and get\n\n$$\n2\\times 2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Eva needs $4$ cups of flour if she wants to use $2$ cups of sugar."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073724 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a94905c-48fe-5662-bb6c-2153f7725648" :knowledge-point/title "Problem Solving Using the Ratio of Two Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a1fb5a4-8ca8-52f6-adf8-f9e8136d4f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$42$ slices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490591} {:answer/id #uuid "6a6fb599-1c48-5edd-8104-02a834687660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$24$ slices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490716} {:answer/id #uuid "7fb22a4d-23b4-5eb7-a1b3-d3564f0b9a94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$28$ slices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490768} {:answer/id #uuid "e1c83694-2906-52a9-9f5b-50a06510fb7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$35$ slices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490939} {:answer/id #uuid "e3b1ff77-affb-5390-aa97-0b625c9a6e43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$21$ slices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fb22a4d-23b4-5eb7-a1b3-d3564f0b9a94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$28$ slices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490768} :answer-field/id #uuid "097611f7-a02a-5f2a-9ad6-dcd9683e52ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "580104c9-cac0-5746-a4a5-7ac914d81f7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-69014" :question/problem "Farhan can buy $2$ slices of pizza for a dollar. If he has $14$ dollars, then how many slices of pizza can he buy?" :question/worked-solution "The unit rate is $2$ slices per dollar. To find the number of slices Farhan can buy for $14$ dollars, we multiply the unit rate by $14$ dollars and get\n\n$$\n2\\times 14=28.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Farhan can buy $28$ slices for $14$ dollars."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea092786-a281-534e-803b-90e6c23b90a9" :knowledge-point/title "Problem Solving Using the Ratio of a Fraction and an Integer"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0310f6ae-86ed-5bcd-8506-b6e65fb54b2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$40$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490517} {:answer/id #uuid "8110aae0-922c-5223-9c2a-82d6828da2ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$25$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490771} {:answer/id #uuid "898375ff-a273-5654-b1a5-b4ae553658aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490785} {:answer/id #uuid "9b90d420-15e0-51d3-9e07-c2cac59126f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490830} {:answer/id #uuid "fb0c21ff-4f96-5117-8019-31abfd00c5c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$32$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0310f6ae-86ed-5bcd-8506-b6e65fb54b2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$40$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490517} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e93abd1-2bd1-5379-bc1e-5642481b5dbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f450169b-fcda-5464-b467-6f84236b6273" :question/math-academy-id "q-69022" :question/problem "Marcel can transcribe $\\frac{3}{8}$ of a paper in $3$ hours. How many hours does it take him to transcribe $5$ papers?" :question/worked-solution "To find the number of hours Marcel takes to transcribe $5$ papers, we can first find the unit rate of hours per paper, and then multiply the unit rate by $5$ papers.\n\nTo find the unit rate of hours per paper, we divide the number of hours, $3,$ by the number of papers, $\\frac{3}{8},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n3÷\\frac{3}{8}\n$$\n\nTo divide by a fraction, we multiply by the fraction's reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3÷\\frac{3}{8} & =3\\times \\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1}\\times \\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 8}{1\\times 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{3} \\\\  & =24÷3 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $8$ hours per paper. To find the number of hours that Marcel takes to transcribe $5$ papers, we multiply the unit rate by $5$ papers and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\times 5 & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Marcel can transcribe $5$ papers in $40$ hours."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/r