ind the number of kilometers that Sophie walks in $2$ hours, we can first find the unit rate of kilometers per hour and multiply the unit rate by $2$ hours.\n\nTo find the unit rate of kilometers per hour, we divide the number of kilometers, $\\frac{3}{5}$, by the number of hours, $\\frac{1}{10}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}÷\\frac{1}{10}\n$$\n\nDividing one fraction by another is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of the second fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}÷\\frac{1}{10} & =\\frac{3}{5}\\times \\frac{10}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\times 10}{5\\times 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{5} \\\\  & =30÷5 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $6$ kilometers per hour. To find the number of kilometers that Sophie walks in $2$ hours, we multiply the unit rate by $2$ hours and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\times 2 & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Sophie walks $12$ kilometers in $2$ hours."}]}
